macOS: count real single waiters before omitting empty kernel notifications.

Cider-Topic: sync/msync
Cider-Requires: 0104-msync-thread-local-fork-admission.patch
Cider-Status: nondefault alternative excluding0105-0109; matching magic6 pair required
Cider-Review-By: independent publication/lifetime/pump-count review and parent
Cider-Test: exact helper,actual shared-ulock parked ABA,wake/count/sticky negatives;
 final library disassembly verifies same-word publication RMW

Keep the original F8 owner,16-byte slots,decision journal,leases,epochs,
state counts/statuses,waits and under-owner kernel notification path. Only omit
notifications when a conservative registered-waiter advertisement proves empty.
Singles publish before compare/park and pop through the existing native wait
registry before frame pins unwind. No new shared reference or thread_data field.
Hard kill may overestimate; the internal count limit selects the original wake
fallback. This never clamps a Windows semaphore or returns a fabricated status.

Pump-owned linked-node counts and temporary advertisements preserve MANY without
erasing singles. Ready-only high indices do not grow the sparse node map. The
extra local node counter costs one unsigned field per allocated map entry.
SC operations modify the same hint word; a harmless PUBLISH bit forces actual
RMW codegen. No correctness depends on its value/wrap period. Invalid internal
count-zero waits cannot borrow an unpinned alert slot; public Windows count-zero
rejection and alertable delay server paths are unchanged.

Native/helper/source checks are not Wine/Windows/game acceptance. Paired runtime,
fixed performance and this exact binary's continuous pressure remain separate.

